  "notes": "Verified 2026-09-17 by fetching the real archived 2022-23 bulletin page directly (bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2022-2023/.../aerospace-engineering-bs/). Suggested Academic Plan, Program Requirements, and total credit requirement (131 credits) are all confirmed identical in shape and sequence to AERSP-2026.json's own corrected placement: EMCH 315/316 are already paired together in 2nd Year Spring/Semester 4 (not split into Semester 5 the way 2026's file described as a bug it had to fix), and the GHW Gen Ed slots already fall in 3rd Year Fall/Semester 5 and 4th Year Fall/Semester 7 -- the archived 2022-23 text never had the two discrepancies AERSP-2026.json's notes describe fixing on 2026-08-27, so nothing needed correcting here. The archived Program Requirements section explicitly states the programming requirement as 'Select 3 credits from CMPSC 121, 131, 200, or 201' -- the same 4-way choice AERSP-2026.json uses, so it is carried forward unchanged (not a 2026-only widening). The archived Program Requirements' First-Year Seminar line reads generically ('First-Year Seminar: 1 credit required', not tied to a specific course code beyond the Suggested Plan's own 'AERSP 1 or 97') -- since this generic framing already existed in the 2022-23 bulletin itself (not just a 2026-dated Faculty Senate policy argument), this file keeps AERSP-2026.json's widened 13-code generic-PSU-FYS option list rather than narrowing it. ME 201 is the only thermal-science option that appears anywhere in the archived bulletin text; ME 300 (2026's Commonwealth-Campus substitute) comes from the department's current, undated curriculum guide PDF, which has no archived per-year equivalent to check, so it is not included here. The archived Program Requirements' Economics line ('Select 3 credits from ECON 102, ECON 104, ECON 14') includes ECON 14, same as the current live bulletin -- this is a constant gap in AERSP-2026.json's own 2-option ECON item (out of scope to correct here), not a year-to-year difference, so this file mirrors AERSP-2026.json's existing ECON 102/104 pair for shape consistency. Technical Elective / General Technical Elective / Limited Elective wiring (regex and lists) is carried forward unchanged from AERSP-2026.json: the archived Program Requirements text lists the same three elective categories at the same credit totals (6 ATE + 3 GTE + 3 LE), and the department's current curriculum guide (the source of 2026's exact denylist/allowlist) has no historical edition to check separately. MATH 21 is retained as the same engine-only prereq-chain fallback AERSP-2026.json uses for CHEM 110 -> MATH 22 -> MATH 21, since Backend/planner_engine.py's course catalog is not year-scoped (the same current catalog data is used to build every catalog year's plan), so this fallback applies uniformly regardless of catalog year.",
